  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let the line intersects the circle at points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></math></p><p>Nw, the given line <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is a diameter as it passes through centre <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3,4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math><mi>O</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0,0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is a point on the circle as <math><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8736;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> as angle in a semi-circle is <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi></math> is perpendicular to <math><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
